      <description align="center" color="yellow" colored="false" height="133" resized="true" width="324" x="186" y="118">Created a separate indicator for each loan type by checking whether it appeared in the customer&amp;#8217;s Type_of_Loan field. This allows customers with multiple loans to be represented by multiple loan items rather than treating each loan combination as a single category.</description>
      <description align="center" color="yellow" colored="false" height="109" resized="true" width="220" x="325" y="340">Converted the loan indicators into binominal true/false values so each loan type represented whether a customer held that product, as required for FP-Growth.</description>
      <description align="center" color="yellow" colored="true" height="94" resized="true" width="179" x="562" y="330">The binary loan indicators were treated as dummy-coded items, with true indicating that the customer held that loan type.</description>
